    pr_ref:  # 97af
    description: "Invariant: `htrac setup` check 22 (`_check_sync_prerequisites`, packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/setup.py ~2739-2784) accepts the token that `htrac sync` actually requires for the repository's origin.\n\nViolated today: the check looks only for FORGEJO_TOKEN. `sync.py` (~1248-1256, ~1302-1305) accepts HG_GITHUB_TOKEN and requires it for a github.com origin, which this repository has.\n\nRepro (docstring-staleness audit 2026-10-17, verifier run): a temp repo with a github origin and only `HG_GITHUB_TOKEN` in `.env`; `_check_sync_prerequisites` returns `warn ... FORGEJO_TOKEN not found`. So setup warns on a correctly configured repo and would pass a github repo that has only a Forgejo token.\n\nRelated: INV-zofog (forge entry scripts reading FORGEJO_TOKEN directly instead of resolving the token by forge). The module docstring (line ~36) describes the current FORGEJO_TOKEN-only behaviour accurately and was left unchanged; update it with the fix to \"the origin's forge token (HG_GITHUB_TOKEN for github, FORGEJO_TOKEN for forgejo)\"."  # 97af
    fields:  # 97af
      statement: "htrac setup's sync-prerequisite check accepts the forge token htrac sync requires for the repository's origin"  # 97af
      root_cause: "_check_sync_prerequisites looks only for FORGEJO_TOKEN; sync.py resolves HG_GITHUB_TOKEN for github origins"  # 97af
