  clock: 3  # b755
  nonce: b755  # b755
  message: "Fixed in PR #1692 (69fc8d9db3). Root cause: setup check 22 kept its own token rule (FORGEJO_TOKEN only) instead of sync's per-forge rule. Fix: one table, sync.FORGE_TOKEN_VARS (github->HG_GITHUB_TOKEN, forgejo->FORGEJO_TOKEN), read by preflight, prune and check 22 with sync's .env parser and messages. Behavioral evidence, re-running the filed repro on merged code: temp repo, origin https://github.com/o/r.git, .env with only HG_GITHUB_TOKEN, both vars unset in the environment -> _check_sync_prerequisites returns 'ok | Sync prerequisites met'; same .env with a codeberg origin -> 'warn | ... FORGEJO_TOKEN not found in .env or environment (required for the forgejo origin)'. Pinned by TestSyncSetupCheckForgeToken (incl. a check-vs-sync agreement test over every backend/token pair). Analogue fixed in the same PR: prune_superseded_sync_branches took HG_GITHUB_TOKEN first on every forge and ignored os.environ (TestPruneTokenFollowsTheOrigin). Related, not covered: INV-zofog (forge entry scripts)."  # b755
